      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5bd570eedbe1156cf5eb1c7e|full_name}: I don't think you understood what I was requesting. With the Index controllers, VRChat will always move the fingers of your avatar to match your hand. But they're also implementing a toggle which allows you to disable gestures. That means if you have animations, sounds, or props tied to a gesture, you can prevent those from triggering by toggling gestures off. All I want is for them to implement the same feature on the Rift, so we too can toggle gesture playback on and off.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
