  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-06-02T19:36:01.022Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I don't know if this is planned or not, but I saw you have a plan to make it so you click the joystick button to disable gestures and enable finger tracking on the Index, and it would be great if you would do the same on the Rift, because even though it does not have full finger tracking, being able to toggle gestures on and off would make it a lot easier to create avatars. Right now I have lots of sounds and props that appear when I do gestures, and sometimes that can get annoying because the more I have the more easy it is to trigger them accidentally. There are work-arounds for this, like using emotes to toggle things on and off, or making an empty object that is on one gesture which has the real object or audio source as a child of it, so you have to hold two gestures to trigger it, but these are complicated to set up. It would no longer be an issue though if I could simply toggle all gestures off with the click of a button! And even though I myself plan to get an index, I do make my avatars public, so having this feature on the Rift as well would be good for everyone who's still using that and using my avatars.",
